    ReportRunsAccessibilityIT. Approved in the security-reviewer role on #121.
    ReportScheduleController (WP-23 part b2): behind login; GET /admin/report-schedules and GET and POST
    /admin/report-schedules/{team}, the POST with CSRF (403 without). ReportScheduleService refuses (403) anyone but
    a Compliance Admin, rebuilding permissions from the database per request, and answers 404 for an unknown team
    (the id parsed leniently to -1) before any input is read. The form binds to a record: the day to the DayOfWeek
    enum, the hour to 0 to 23 (anything else is a 422 with the form marked), the version parsed leniently (anything
    unreadable is stale); the service re-checks the hour and saves only at the version the form was loaded with,
    flushing inside its transaction so a concurrent save, a delivery or a second first save is a 409 with Reload, never
    a lost update. Each save is audited as REPORT_SCHEDULE_CHANGED, old to new. The redirect is the fixed path
    /admin/report-schedules; team names are echoed through th:text. Covered by ReportScheduleIT,
    OracleReportScheduleIT, ReportScheduleControllerIT and ReportSchedulesAccessibilityIT.
